WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.170
A ball flies towards you.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.250
You track it, reach out and catch it.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.480
Light from the ball enters your eyes,
right at the front of your head.

4
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.000
Somewhere inside your head, that
light becomes something you can see.

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.750
So which part of your
brain did the seeing?

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.670
The part nearest your eyes?

7
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.590
In this mission, you'll map the
wrinkled outer layer of your brain,

8
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.980
the cerebral cortex:
four lobes in each half,

9
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.240
plus the cerebellum underneath.

10
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.880
Each part has its own main jobs.

11
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.570
One of them fine-tunes your movements, so
you reach for the ball without missing.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: work out which part of
your brain turns light into sight.
